//! The published FairPlay v3 key-derivation vectors.
//!
//! Twenty `(key message, ekey, expected key)` triples covering all four modes,
//! taken from the reference implementation's own test data. They are what makes a
//! from-scratch transcription verifiable without a live capture: the derivation is
//! four hundred lines of bit manipulation that would otherwise fail silently, by
//! producing a wrong key and a mirroring session that shows static.
//!
//! Fixtures, not a dependency (ground rule 9) — the bytes are checked in here.

use crypto_playfair::{decrypt_key, EKEY_LEN, KEY_MESSAGE_LEN};

